/*
 * Houseplants and indoor succulents/cacti. Toxicity flags are our own yes/no reading of the ASPCA list (cats and dogs);
 * the app links out to ASPCA for detail and never copies its text. Where ASPCA has no listing for the exact species,
 * a comment says so and how we decided: aroids, euphorbias and lilies are treated as toxic; other plants follow
 * their listed genus/family when ASPCA lists close relatives.
 * `art` is the illustrated buddy shown for the plant: its own, or the closest look-alike until it gets one.
 *
 * Photo-ID matching (src/lib/plantId.ts): `match.species` = exact synonyms, `match.genus` = this entry stands for the
 * whole genus, `match.relatives` = close relatives only. Each genus is claimed by at most one entry.
 */
